# ── Discord integration (server-only) ──────────────────────────
# Everything here is read ONLY by server code (lib/discord.js,
# lib/discord-token-store.mjs, API routes). NEVER prefix these with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ and NEVER import them into client components —
# `import "server-only"` in lib/discord.js enforces this at build
# time for the main boundary.
#
# TWO KINDS OF SECRETS — do not mix them:
#
#   STATIC CONFIG (set once, changes never):
#     DISCORD_CLIENT_ID / DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET / DISCORD_REDIRECT_URI
#
#   ROTATING SECRET (Discord replaces it on most refresh grants):
#     lives in the persistent token store below. DISCORD_REFRESH_TOKEN
#     remains ONLY as the initial seed for pre-existing deployments;
#     once the store is seeded, rotations save themselves and the env
#     value is ignored until the store is ever empty again.
#
# Setup (one time, owner only):
#   1. https://discord.com/developers → New Application → OAuth2.
#   2. Add a redirect URL exactly matching DISCORD_REDIRECT_URI, e.g.
#      https://your-domain.vercel.app/api/auth/discord/callback
#      (local: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/discord/callback)
#   3. Set the static variables, attach an Upstash Redis database
#      (Vercel → Storage → Marketplace → Upstash Redis) so the two
#      UPSTASH_* variables below are provisioned, then redeploy.
#   4. Open /setup/discord (unlinked route), authorize (identify
#      scope only). The refresh token stores itself — no copying,
#      no second redeploy. Done — visitors never log in.
#   5. If Discord ever rejects the stored token (revoked), the site
#      keeps rendering from cache and /setup/discord says so:
#      authorize once more and the store reseeds.
#
# Recovery for the pre-store era: the old manually-saved
# DISCORD_REFRESH_TOKEN (if still valid) seeds the store on the
# next successful exchange. If it already 400s, just re-authorize.

# Public identifier of your Discord application (not a secret, but
# keep it server-side with the rest for a clean boundary).
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=

# OAuth client secret — SECRET. Server env only, never commit.
# DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Must match a redirect URL registered in the Discord portal.
# DISCORD_REDIRECT_URI=

# Owner refresh token — SECRET + INITIAL SEED ONLY.
# Keep this set (harmless once the store is seeded): it is the
# migration path for deployments predating the persistent store.
# Runtime mints short-lived access tokens from the stored token;
# access tokens are never stored, logged, or sent to the browser.
# DISCORD_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Persistent token store — provisioned automatically when you attach
# Upstash Redis in Vercel. Server-only. This is what makes rotation
# survive cold starts, sibling instances, and deployments.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Resolves the site owner's account. Public constant, safe here.
# DISCORD_USER_ID=920627516694200360
